  "plain": "In the 1980s, after Ronald Reagan became president, a writer named Bill Sweetman is said to have made a deep study of special access programs, the most tightly sealed secret projects in the US military, and of how they were split apart and sometimes duplicated. A researcher named Eric W. Davis mentions this to Michels from memory, saying he thinks it was Sweetman, and he raises it to show how hidden programs can be walled off so that even insiders do not see the whole picture."
